From 5a9551562879c98123b39d75cca4732d159f541c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:07:04 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(post): Tormach programs end at the top of Z - no trailing
 G30

The Tormach mill post ended M9, M5, G53 G0 Z0, G30, M30. A bare G30
moves every axis to the stored G30 position, so in the user's PathPilot
Hub run (770MX sim, stored G30 at machine Z -1.5611) the end lifted to
the top of travel and then drove the tool back down below the part top.
The program now ends at the lift: M5, G53 G0 Z0 (or the machine's stated
safe Z, #495), the EndUnits word if any (#596), M30. No G0 A0 is added.
The G30 before each tool change is unchanged: retract() keeps it, the end
uses the new liftZ() alone.

The 33 Tormach mill NC goldens lose their last G30 line and nothing else.
Pinned by tormach_program_end (every shipped Tormach mill, a stated safe
Z, a 4th-axis job), with tormach_post / tormach_safe_retract /
tormach_end_units updated to the new ending.

Fixes #1594

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
